WEBVTT

00:08:57.720 --> 00:09:01.087
"Alright, if this thing
starts erupting right now,

00:09:01.111 --> 00:09:02.844
what's our exit strategy?"

00:09:03.269 --> 00:09:06.412
And he said, "Oh, yeah,
great question, it's totally easy.

00:09:06.436 --> 00:09:09.514
Just turn around and enjoy the view."

00:09:09.538 --> 00:09:10.831
(Laughter)

00:09:10.855 --> 00:09:12.402
"Because it will be your last."

00:09:12.426 --> 00:09:13.561
(Laughter)

00:09:13.585 --> 00:09:17.030
And it may sound like
he was being overly dramatic,

00:09:17.054 --> 00:09:21.807
but 54 days after I was standing
next to that lake,

00:09:21.831 --> 00:09:23.252
this happened.

00:09:23.276 --> 00:09:24.434
Audience: Oh!

00:09:25.204 --> 00:09:26.854
Freaking terrifying, right?

00:09:26.878 --> 00:09:28.028
(Laughs)

00:09:28.934 --> 00:09:33.287
This was the biggest eruption
this volcano had had in 60-some-odd years,